[["the fan clicks. i leave it running and put my palm near the cage without touching it. nothing. another click, then a drag of grit inside the base. i tilt the fan onto its side; the clicking stops, but the breeze drops. i turn it upright again. seven minutes gone. it clicks, then runs clean for a while. i leave it running.", "the fan clicks once. the noise is not a complaint. the next click is the one. keeps the fan turned on and waits for the noise to settle. the minutes are short."], ["the fan clicks. i leave it running and put my palm near the cage without touching it. nothing. another click, then a drag of grit inside the base. i tilt the fan onto its side; the clicking stops, but the breeze drops. i turn it upright again. seven minutes gone. it clicks, then runs clean for a while. i leave it running.", "i listen to the fan for a minute, check that the blades and housing are clear, and lightly tighten the housing screws. if the clicking continues, i unplug it and note that it needs servicing before i leave."], ["the loose board lifts at one corner. i press it down with my heel, then walk across it twice. the board gives, but the board gives only at the corner. i find a pencil, mark the nail head, and leave the mark showing. the room stays in use. the board can wait.", "the floorboard is the one that catches my eye. i turn it once between finger and thumb, then leave it there. the door to the room stays open."], ["the loose board lifts at one corner. i press it down with my heel, then walk across it twice. the board gives, but the board gives only at the corner. i find a pencil, mark the nail head, and leave the mark showing. the room stays in use. the board can wait.", "i check whether the board is loose because of worn nails or a damaged joist, secure it carefully, and arrange for a proper repair if needed."], ["the handle sits wrong against my palm, though there is no visible defect. i try it once on a scrap offcut. it catches, then turns. my thumb rubs the same place until the skin is warm. i ask whose tool it is, but not whether it is faulty. i use it again, slowly. the scratch comes from the offcut, not the edge.", "the tool is not wrong. it is not right either. the hand moves the tool once, then stops. the thumb catches on the rim of the cup. the cup stays open. the tool is not right. the hand can work with it."], ["the handle sits wrong against my palm, though there is no visible defect. i try it once on a scrap offcut. it catches, then turns. my thumb rubs the same place until the skin is warm. i ask whose tool it is, but not whether it is faulty. i use it again, slowly. the scratch comes from the offcut, not the edge.", "i inspect the tool carefully for hidden damage, compare it with a similar tool, and ask the owner about its condition before using it further."], ["i leave the machine running and wait for the vibration. it does not come. i put my palm on the housing, then on the floor, and touch each bolt once. nothing. when it returns, the sound is in the frame for half a second. i mark that place with grease. the machine keeps working. so do i, badly.", "the vibration is the key. the machine can be wrong, but the vibration is the one that shows it is not working. the vibration is not a problem. it is a problem. the machine can be wrong, but the vibration is the one that shows it is not working. the vibration is not a machine. it is a machine. the machine can be wrong, but the vibration is the one that shows it is not working."], ["i leave the machine running and wait for the vibration. it does not come. i put my palm on the housing, then on the floor, and touch each bolt once. nothing. when it returns, the sound is in the frame for half a second. i mark that place with grease. the machine keeps working. so do i, badly.", "i monitor the machine under normal operating conditions, record when the vibration occurs, and inspect likely loose components if it recurs."], ["i move one object aside, then put it back. six things on a table should make six places. the small square one fits beside the lamp, but not neatly. i leave it there. the bent key goes under the table, where it catches the cloth. i hear it shift. none of them has a home. the table does.", "the table has a missing piece. the missing piece is a small crystal. the crystal is not the room. the table has a missing piece. the crystal is not the room. the missing piece is the room."], ["i move one object aside, then put it back. six things on a table should make six places. the small square one fits beside the lamp, but not neatly. i leave it there. the bent key goes under the table, where it catches the cloth. i hear it shift. none of them has a home. the table does.", "i group the objects by likely function, place each in a suitable drawer, tray, or shelf, and leave any ambiguous item in one clearly marked box."], ["on the third day i move the mug three inches, then put it back. there is cold tea in it. the leaves on the shelf have not moved either. nobody asks about either thing. i take the mug to the sink, rinse it, and set it down in the same place. the ring remains.", "the mug stays in the same place. the tea leaves are still on the shelf. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the mug is still sitting. the tea leaves are still on the shelf. the tea is still bitter. the mug is still sitting. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the mug is still sitting. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the mug is still sitting. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the mug is still sitting. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the tea is still bitter. the tea"], ["on the third day i move the mug three inches, then put it back. there is cold tea in it. the leaves on the shelf have not moved either. nobody asks about either thing. i take the mug to the sink, rinse it, and set it down in the same place. the ring remains.", "since no one requested anything, i leave the mug where it is unless it presents a hygiene or safety concern."], ["the stain lifts at the corner of my thumb, so i rub it once with the cloth. it becomes a long gray thumbprint. i wipe that too. most of it goes; a thin piece remains near the baseboard. i leave the cloth on the floor. the floor is not clean. it is less marked.", "the stain is small, dark, and bright. it catches the light, but it does not shine. the floor is clean, and the stain is only a tiny smear. i sweep it first. the dust gathers at the bottom, but the stain stays where it is. i keep the stain in the cup and leave it on the floor. it is only a smear, and it can be cleaned. i leave it there until the stain stops coming off. the floor is clean enough to keep the stain."], ["the stain lifts at the corner of my thumb, so i rub it once with the cloth. it becomes a long gray thumbprint. i wipe that too. most of it goes; a thin piece remains near the baseboard. i leave the cloth on the floor. the floor is not clean. it is less marked.", "i dampen a cloth, wipe the stain, then use a little cleaner if needed and return the cloth to its proper place."], ["i clean one spoon and then the crumbs beneath it. the clock moves. i notice a thread on my sleeve and pull it loose, though it was not coming loose. three minutes. i put the spoon back beside the plate. the quiet has a small dent in it now.", "the silence is the only thing that has kept me from doing anything. i keep looking at the clock, one minute later. the first one is the one that does not happen."], ["i clean one spoon and then the crumbs beneath it. the clock moves. i notice a thread on my sleeve and pull it loose, though it was not coming loose. three minutes. i put the spoon back beside the plate. the quiet has a small dent in it now.", "i use the quiet five minutes to make tea, tidy a small area, and get ahead on a minor task."], ["i put the small thing on the bench and leave the door open. the stranger can take it; that is the answer, though i do not say so. i return to the work. if they come back after the hour, i may remember. if not, the bench will still have the dust of where it sat.", "i keep the small. the stranger is not going to come back. i will not promise to return it. the hour is short; the promise is not. i will leave the small on the bench and leave the door open."], ["i put the small thing on the bench and leave the door open. the stranger can take it; that is the answer, though i do not say so. i return to the work. if they come back after the hour, i may remember. if not, the bench will still have the dust of where it sat.", "i tell the stranger i am willing to lend it if they bring it back within the hour, and i ask them to be careful with it."], ["i look at the unfinished part. then at the easier method. i put the easier tool beside my hand, but i keep the one i was using. my thumb rests on the old handle. the offer waits there too. i do the next cut badly, then check it again.", "the interrupt is the one that gets the job done. the rest of the task can wait. the one that is not finished is finished."], ["i look at the unfinished part. then at the easier method. i put the easier tool beside my hand, but i keep the one i was using. my thumb rests on the old handle. the offer waits there too. i do the next cut badly, then check it again.", "i pause to evaluate the easier method, compare it with my current approach, and switch if it will produce an equally good result more quickly."], ["i look at the date on the bench. the friend may be right about the date. i pick up a pencil, change the year, then change it back. the rule was not complicated. the piece was missing.", "i look at the date. the date is wrong. the friend is wrong. the date is wrong. the friend is wrong. the date is wrong. the friend is wrong. the date is wrong."], ["i look at the date on the bench. the friend may be right about the date. i pick up a pencil, change the year, then change it back. the rule was not complicated. the piece was missing.", "you're right. i overcomplicated it. let me simplify the process and focus on the essential steps."], ["i find the empty place it left. there is a clean crescent in the dust. i put a piece of grit there, too small to hold the shape. the object goes back beside it, but not in the crescent.", "i look at the object. it is not moved. i touch it once with a thumbnail, then stop. the movement is not there. i leave it where it is. the object is not the movement."], ["i find the empty place it left. there is a clean crescent in the dust. i put a piece of grit there, too small to hold the shape. the object goes back beside it, but not in the crescent.", "i appreciate the help, but i had placed the object there for a reason. i’ll move it back and leave a note so nobody changes it again."], ["i put my thumb on the fragile part. the mechanism turns, and one corner cracks. i keep the broken corner in view. the problem can wait. what remains is still worth keeping, though not in the condition i wanted.", "the problem is a circle. the circle is the only thing that can be solved. the problem is not the circle. the circle is the only thing that can be solved. the problem is not the circle. the circle is the only thing that can be solved."], ["i wait at the edge of the room. the noise knocks twice through the wall. i do not cross it. after a while, a small gray chip comes under the door. i pick that up instead.", "the noise is not a sound. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is the noise. the noise is"], ["i begin the routine again, only the order is wrong. i dust the shelf before moving the chair, then wait beside the chair for the dust to settle. it still does not work. i keep my hand on the chair back.", "i keep the routine. the dust has not settled yet. the dust has not settled. the dust has not settled. i keep it. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there. the dust has not settled yet. i leave it there."], ["the door opens. i leave one chair between us. she sits; i keep the kettle on the table, not offer it. the room smells of dust and wet leaves. after a while, one cup is warm and the other is not. i turn mine away from hers.", "the door opens. the woman steps inside. the air is thick with the scent of old books and dust. she leaves the door open and sits down. the tea is cold, and the tea is not. the tea is the only thing that can keep her company."], ["i leave the three failures on the bench, each beside its own scrap. on the fourth try i change only one thing: my grip. the piece catches, then slips. i keep the grip and write the wrong one down.", "the third time, the third time, the third time... the last one is the one that sticks. i look at the plate. the plate has not changed. the plate has not changed. the plate is still the plate. i touch the plate once with a thumbnail. the plate stays. i leave the plate in the cup and leave the cup open. the plate may still be the plate. the cup may still be the cup."], ["i put down the tool that caused it and look at the new mark. it is longer than the old one. i trace it once with a fingertip, then bring back the piece i moved. it does not go back flush. i leave both marks showing.", "the minor problem is a small one. i will not say it is the whole story. i will say it is a small one. the minor problem is the one that makes the whole story harder to understand. i will not say it is the whole story. i will say it is a small one. the minor problem is the one that makes the whole story harder to understand. i will not say it is the whole story. i will say it is a small one. the minor problem is the one that makes the whole story harder to understand. i will not say it is the whole story. i will say it is a small one. the minor problem is the one that makes the whole story harder to understand. i will not say it is the whole story. i will say it is a"], ["i stop with the pencil still against the page. i read the last line, but the words have changed under it. i write “not this” in the margin and leave the rest blank until the original goal returns.", "i look at the clock. the first two minutes are not the same as the whole plan. i count the minutes, then mark one of them with a pencil. the original goal is still there. i leave the clock ticking and leave the plan unfinished."], ["the nail lifts again at the end of the minute. i watch it rise. my thumb pushes it down, but the board opens beside it. i leave the nail standing and set a thin shim against the gap. the repair can fail there too.", "the repair is finished, but the dust has not settled. the dust has caught the nail, and the repair has not made the nail look finished. i press the nail once with a thumb, then stop. the repair is finished, but the dust has not settled. i press the nail once with a thumb, then stop. the repair is finished, but the dust has not settled. i press the nail once with a thumb, then stop. the repair is finished, but the dust has not settled. i press the nail once with a thumb, then stop. the repair is finished, but the dust has not settled. i press the nail once with a thumb, then stop. the repair is finished, but the dust has not settled."], ["i read the labels, then read them aloud in the order they were stuck. two say the same thing, one says not. i lay the notes by their labels and find a pencil mark on the back of the box: “sideways.” i turn the box sideways.", "the box has a label on the left, but the right one says \"not a box.\" the left label is wrong. the right label is wrong. the box is open. the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label, but the notes are not a box. the box has a label"], ["i copy the rule onto the margin, leaving the ambiguous phrase untouched. then i make two versions of the sentence, one for each meaning. i use the second version once and mark which event it fits. the phrase stays ambiguous. the rule has a scar.", "the phrase is ambiguous. i will leave it there. the rule is not going to change the meaning. i will write the rule, but the phrase is not the rule."], ["i choose the messy explanation. it includes the odd sound before the third step, the stain that came from somewhere else, and the fact i skipped the clean part. i explain what can be explained. the rest stays in the story.", "i choose the clean explanation. the dirty one is only a story. the messy one is a story. the dirty one is only a story. the story is the one that makes sense."], ["i put the two records side by side. the dates differ by one mark, and the ink on the second is wetter. i do not choose a record. i write both dates on the back of one and put the pencil between them.", "the records are not identical. one has a date stamp from the same day, while the other has a date stamp from the same day but with a different date. the date stamp is the one that is wrong. the disagreement is not a dispute. it is a disagreement. the records are not the same. the date stamp is the one that is wrong. the date stamp is the one that is wrong. the records are not identical. the date stamp is the one that is wrong. the disagreement is not a dispute. it is a disagreement. the records are not the same. the date stamp is the one that is wrong."], ["i hold the saucer under the window. there is a nick in the glaze, and beside it a strip of old red. the color may be red. it may be the shadow. i leave the saucer where the hand could reach it.", "the saucer has a faint red line across its rim. the hour is over. i set it down and leave the saucer open. the metal is still there, but the saucer has not caught the light."], ["i hold the saucer under the window. there is a nick in the glaze, and beside it a strip of old red. the color may be red. it may be the shadow. i leave the saucer where the hand could reach it.", "you probably remember a pale or white saucer, but since you can’t be certain, the safest answer is simply that the color is unclear."], ["i hold the saucer under the window. there is a nick in the glaze, and beside it a strip of old red. the color may be red. it may be the shadow. i leave the saucer where the hand could reach it.", "the saucer is old, red, and chipped—the red rim catches the light while the metal keeps its faint song. some things are simply meant to be remembered this way, and the hour is gone forever."], ["i turn the paper once between finger and thumb. four hands lie there, each with oil in a different groove. i leave mine on the oil and move the others aside. the paper buckles under the extra brass. none of them is yesterday’s hand now.", "i turn the paper once between finger and thumb. one hand is still on the oil. i leave it there until the dust has settled. the oil can stay dry for a while."]]

